{"content":[{"c":["BLOOD, F",{"c":["ield of"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"}],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name given to the field purchased with the “blood money” Judas accepted to betray Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.8","r":"Matt.27.8","rawR":"Matt.27.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.8","value":"Matt.27.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.1.19","r":"Acts.1.19","rawR":"Acts.1.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.1.19","value":"Acts.1.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 1:19"},"). The field was purchased by the chief priests as a burial ground for strangers (formerly, the potter’s field). Judas hanged himself and his intestines burst open there. This account uses the Aramaic expression ",{"c":["Akeldama"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Aceldama”), translated “field of blood.” The Akeldama is situated on the southern slope of the valley of Hinnom near the Kidron Valley."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BloodFieldof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mt 27:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.8","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.8","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.8"},{"anchorText":"Acts 1:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.1.19","rawQueryValue":"Acts.1.19","sourceRefExact":"Acts.1.19"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b1194e84d349276b24a1d3c8b5c20a901ce8b6f85709123b0566d41c54fa3732","sourceItemName":"BloodFieldof","sourceItemOrder":348,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BloodFieldof","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Blood, Field of","title":"Blood, Field of","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}